# Offline and desktop apps


::divider{aqua}
## Working offline

Radii Office saves itself for offline use the first time you visit. After that, the apps open without a connection, and your documents are already on your computer. When you are back online, nothing needs to be synced because nothing left your computer!

Things that need the internet by nature, like Phosphor chat, Beta, Mintcode, Overshare and getting real email in Yuzu, only work online. Everything that edits your own files works offline!

## Installing

* ++TU5)As an app from the browser.++ In Chrome or Edge, use the install button in the address bar to add an app to your dock or desktop!
* ~~TU=Desktop apps.~~ Open [Products](/products) and press %%C+Download%% on any app for a Mac, Windows or Linux build. Desktop apps open and save files directly on your computer, and they are rebuilt whenever the site changes!
* @retrodesk-1@Phones.@ Most apps have a **Mobile** button that opens a layout designed for small screens!

## Checking downloads

Downloads are signed so you can check that nobody changed them. The public keys and fingerprints are in `/signing/` on this site, and the pages have integrity hashes on their scripts. The details are in [Privacy and security](#/security)!

## Open files from your computer

In any app, use **File > Open** to pick a file from your computer. Desktop apps can open and save files directly on disk!
